      "message": "Since common_intel_x86_power_handle_state() is not called until the end of this function, it tries to power on here before getting to that check, fails, and goes back to G3. See the logs in b/271534947#comment12. CL:1980104 duplicated the intel_x86_wait_power_up_ok() check in the same way, since cometlake-discrete also calls common_intel_x86_power_handle_state() at the end of power_handle_state(). Let me know if you think there\u0027s a better way to solve this.\n\nCONFIG_CHARGER_MIN_POWER_MW_FOR_POWER_ON is set to 16 W in dibbi/board.h, but without this change it tries to power on with less than that.",
